To solve this, we first find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 84 and 144. The GCD of 84 and 144 is 12. Then, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the GCD. So,
\begin{align*}
Human & \to \color{magenta}{\frac{144}{144}=1} \\
Rat & \to \color{magenta}{\frac{84}{144}=\frac{84\div 12}{144\div 12}=\frac{7}{12}}
\end{align*>
</think> <answer>$\frac{7}{12}$</answer>

